WHAT YOU MAY DO

1. Read the course, run the notebooks and the course library, and learn from them, for your own
   study or for teaching, as long as learners are pointed to the original site or repository.
2. Link to any page of the site or any file in the repository.
3. Quote short passages with clear credit to Shreyan Basu Ray and a link to the source.
4. Open issues and pull requests on this repository to report bugs or contribute. Forks made on
   GitHub for that purpose are allowed, as the GitHub Terms of Service require.
5. Use the ideas you learn here, such as unlearning methods and audit techniques, in your own work.
   Ideas are not owned. This licence protects the way this course expresses and presents them.

WHAT YOU MAY NOT DO WITHOUT WRITTEN PERMISSION

